tring\",\n            \"description\": \"Category.\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"groceries\",\n              \"rent\",\n              \"travel\",\n              \"utilities\",\n              \"salary\",\n              \"other\"\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"start_date\",\n        \"end_date\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Banking_1_TransferMoney\",\n    \"description\": \"Transfer money from one of the user's accounts to another account number, executed immediately.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"amount\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\",\n          \"description\": \"Amount to transfer in the account currency, e.g. 125.5.\"\n        },\n        \"recipient_account\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Recipient's account number or IBAN, exactly as given.\"\n        },\n        \"account_type\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Which of the user's accounts to use.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"checking\",\n            \"savings\"\n          ],\n          \"default\": \"checking\"\n        },\n        \"memo\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Reference text the recipient sees on their statement.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"amount\",\n        \"recipient_account\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: How much is in my savings account?\n\nReply with only a JSON array of the tool calls that fulfil the request, each of the form {\"name\": \"<tool name>\", \"arguments\": {...}}, where \"arguments\" is a JSON object (not a string). When the request needs several calls, list them all. Reply with [] if no tool fits the request, or if the request does not give a value for a required argument: never guess one. Include every required argument. Include an optional argument only if the request asks for a value for it; otherwise leave it out and the tool applies its default. Give each value the type its schema declares: JSON numbers for integer and number, true or false for boolean, and strings for string, copied exactly as written.","role":"user"},{"content":"[{\"name\":\"Banking_1_CheckBalance\",\"arguments\":{\"account_type\":\"savings\"}}]","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool results:\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Banking_1_CheckBalance\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"account_type\": \"savings\",\n      \"balance\": 6421.85,\n      \"currency\": \"EUR\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: Move 171 of it to NL26BANK0261781726, reference \"Tuition\".\n\nReply as before: only a JSON array of tool calls, or [] if no tool fits or a required value is missing.","role":"user"}]